// Original court story. Hugh knows the histories and the stewards, not the regalia.
export const COURT_DIALOGUE={
 scout:[['Agnes de Clare','Keep your partners on the pale stones. The roots have lifted half the old road.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','Are you with the expedition?','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','Sir Hugh’s scout. De Mowbray, not the miller. There are two Hughs in these woods and neither enjoys the mistake.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Agnes de Clare','He spent years matching broken rolls to old carvings. Thirteen feline stewards, each carrying a Mark of Honour for its own kind. Karolion led them. They protected their type’s Abyssals and kept the elements from overwhelming one another.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','And Hugh wants them for the First Light?','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','He wants the First Light to deserve its name again. He is the most pious man I know. That makes the seized grain and the burned villages harder for him to stomach, not easier. He thinks the old court might teach our knights chivalry.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Agnes de Clare','The Common Cause followed our tracks. Darius has heard enough about the stewards to want them for a different lesson. His people hold the clearings. I got this arm trying to bring the pack back.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','What is beyond the trees?','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','Hugh could not tell me. The histories describe duties, not treasures. The trials still work, though. Read what the keepers left. Forcing your way through will teach you nothing.','CHR-COURT-AGNES']],
 monument:[['Broken royal monument','Thirteen Marks around one tempered crown. Below it: “Let each shelter their own kind, and hold their power within its bounds.”'],['Aimon','A rule for the guardians. Not a claim on everything they guarded.','CHR-AIMON']],
 banner:[['Torn banner','An old embroidered motto survives beneath the First Light badge: “Before obedience, duty. Before triumph, care.”'],['Agnes’s annotation','Hugh copied this before he made camp. He said the modern oath had lost the first line.']],
 orders:[['Expedition notes','The Shared Spring and the paired wardens are duties made into mechanisms. The six Marks at the inner arch answer only when the whole oath is right. No relief names every step. Compare all three with the stewards’ record. — H. de Mowbray'],['Aimon','He worked out what the tests meant. He still left the work for whoever followed.','CHR-AIMON']],
 footprints:[['Scored paving','Grass has grown through old paw marks. A carved Fire guardian faces an Ice guardian across the broken procession. Neither is shown kneeling.']],
 camp:[['Agnes de Clare','Sit your living partners by the spring. I can clean their wounds and refill their water. The dead are beyond anything in this pack.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','Hugh went on alone?','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','With his partners. He still says a knight must go first where he asks others to follow. Darius has crossed behind him. His people are bringing their wounded back through this ravine.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Agnes de Clare','I will keep this camp open. Beyond it you still have a rear guard, Darius and Hugh to face. Take the time you need.','CHR-COURT-AGNES']],
 roots:[['Carving beneath the roots','The stewards held flood, winter, flame and storm in their bounds. No element was cast out; no type was made lesser. Their Marks honoured service under Karolion, whose crown answered to the same oath.']],
 fieldNotes:[['Sir Hugh’s field notes','The marks in the rolls match these ruins. I believe the thirteen were real. I do not know what waits in the sealed chamber. If I find them, I must ask them to judge what our order has become. I cannot claim their honour for us.'],['Aimon','No list of treasure. No claim to a throne. Just a question he wants answered.','CHR-AIMON']],
 throne:[['Empty throne','Thirteen paw-shaped hollows surround the seat. An orb and a sceptre rest in an untouched cradle beneath it. None of Hugh’s sketches shows them.']],
 regalia:[['Aimon','An orb, and a sceptre. They are untouched. Hugh’s notes said nothing about these.','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','I have never seen either. The shapes in the orb—are those the stewards?','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','Thirteen of them. The light tightens every time I touch the cradle.','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','Then be careful. We have reached the end of his research.','CHR-COURT-AGNES']],
 freed:[['Aimon','They were held here. Lifting the regalia opened the binding.','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','All those years in his books, and Hugh never knew. Look at them. Not one is waiting for an order.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['Aimon','Karolion is letting the others choose their own way.','CHR-AIMON'],['Agnes de Clare','Then perhaps that is the first lesson we take back. Tell Hugh what happened. Tell Darius too, if he will listen.','CHR-COURT-AGNES'],['The court is roaming','The thirteen unique stewards can now appear on any eligible route, with a shared 1% encounter chance. Each may flee after a round. A guardian captured or killed never appears again.']],
 repeat:[['Agnes de Clare','Their Marks were duties, not brands. If one chooses to follow you, remember the difference.','CHR-COURT-AGNES']]
};
